WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.483
An installation record should make the
comparison understandable.

2
00:00:04.603 --> 00:00:08.258
For the valve identity check, record the
actual model

3
00:00:08.378 --> 00:00:11.757
and tag, the referenced schedule and the
outcome.

4
00:00:11.877 --> 00:00:15.257
A tick without the required observation
may leave

5
00:00:15.377 --> 00:00:18.549
a reviewer unable to reconstruct the
decision.

6
00:00:18.669 --> 00:00:21.497
Use the approved form and record the work

7
00:00:21.617 --> 00:00:25.410
when performed, not from memory at the end
of the week.

8
00:00:26.030 --> 00:00:28.720
A photograph can support an observation

9
00:00:28.840 --> 00:00:31.253
if the relevant feature is readable

10
00:00:31.373 --> 00:00:34.339
and its relationship to the check is
clear.

11
00:00:34.459 --> 00:00:38.804
Record location, subject and the
controlled evidence reference.

12
00:00:38.924 --> 00:00:40.924
A cropped image of a plate

13
00:00:41.044 --> 00:00:44.285
without the equipment context may be
ambiguous.

14
00:00:44.405 --> 00:00:48.957
Photographs supplement the specified
verification method; they are

15
00:00:49.077 --> 00:00:53.698
not automatically sufficient for every
installation characteristic.

16
00:00:54.318 --> 00:00:58.731
Suppose a handwritten serial number
contains a transposed digit.

17
00:00:58.851 --> 00:01:02.576
Correct it using the approved
documentation procedure,

18
00:01:02.696 --> 00:01:04.744
preserving the original entry

19
00:01:04.864 --> 00:01:07.484
and recording the required attribution

20
00:01:07.604 --> 00:01:10.501
and date, with a reason where appropriate.

21
00:01:10.621 --> 00:01:14.276
Do not erase the original or backdate the
correction.

22
00:01:14.396 --> 00:01:18.327
For electronic records, use the controlled
system process

23
00:01:18.447 --> 00:01:21.344
rather than an untracked replacement file.

24
00:01:21.464 --> 00:01:24.705
Retain original records, printouts,
photographs

25
00:01:24.825 --> 00:01:29.032
and raw electronic data under the defined
retention schedule,

26
00:01:29.152 --> 00:01:32.669
with controlled locations and integrity
safeguards.

27
00:01:32.789 --> 00:01:36.582
The applicable period depends on the
supported activity

28
00:01:36.702 --> 00:01:42.206
and regulatory obligations; this exercise
sets no universal number of years.

29
00:01:42.826 --> 00:01:47.102
Not applicable, not checked and failed are
different statuses.

30
00:01:47.222 --> 00:01:50.050
A check outside the approved system scope

31
00:01:50.170 --> 00:01:52.860
needs a justified not-applicable basis.

32
00:01:52.980 --> 00:01:55.669
An inaccessible feature is not checked.

33
00:01:55.789 --> 00:01:58.371
A verified mismatch is a discrepancy.

34
00:01:58.491 --> 00:02:02.629
Keeping these statuses distinct prevents a
completed-looking

35
00:02:02.749 --> 00:02:06.749
form from implying that evidence exists
where it does not.
